ult)**: Succeeds only for current unexpired lease and active task, exactly once. Checks: task must be queued/running, current lease must exist, token must match, lease must not be expired (now - claimed_at > ttl), result must not already be published. Returns True on success, False otherwise. Stores deep copy of result for owner.\n\n- **results(owner)**: Returns completed results for that owner in submission order as a deep copy (including nested result dictionaries).\n\nAll operations are thread-safe using a single threading.Lock(). No disk/network dependencies.\n\nChecks performed against the implementation:\n- submit basic: duplicate active returns same id, after cancel allows new id\n- submit different keys returns different ids\n- claim queued task returns correct lease dict\n- claim respects insertion order\n- each claim uses new unique fencing token\n- cancel own task succeeds\n- cancel another owner raises PermissionError\n- cancel missing task returns False\n- cancel terminal task returns False\n- publish succeeds with correct lease and token\n- publish fails with wrong token\n- publish fails with expired lease\n- publish fails with stale/expired worker\n- publish exactly once (second publish returns False)\n- results returns deep copy; modifying copy doesn't affect original\n- results returns empty list for owner with no completed tasks\n- claim expired running task is eligible again\n- ttl=0 from claim returns None\n- concurrent submit access works without errors\n\nThe implementation was written to the workspace engine.py file. No smoke_test.py or other fixture files were modified.", "tests_passed": true, "action": "final"}, "tool_mode": "native", "native_tool_calls": 33, "format_errors": 0, "code_pass": false, "acceptance": {"success": false, "exit_code": 1, "output": "", "error": "Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<bench>\\light_worker.py\", line 114, in <module>\n    execute(root,task,checks)\n    ~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"<bench>